  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_16093",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Olaparib may be associated with Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary through a pathway involving Altretamine. Both Olaparib and Altretamine are indicated for Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Immature Ovarian Teratoma, which are both classified as borderline epithelial tumors. This indicates a potential shared therapeutic target or mechanism of action between these entities. The presence of Altretamine as a common indication across different tumor types suggests a possible role in the treatment of borderline epithelial tumors, possibly through a common pathway or mechanism. The scores from the paths, although not directly indicating a causal relationship, suggest a level of association that may warrant further investigation into the biological mechanisms underlying this connection.",
